      "worked_solution": "Since all points $P(x,y)$ in our set lie at integer values of $x$ and $y,$ we have $x\\in Z,y\\in Z,$ and therefore \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\in Z\\times Z={Z}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe points in our set include all those that lie *to the left* the line $x=2.$ For those points, the following condition is satisfied:\n\n$$\nx<2\n$$\n\nSince the boundary is *not* included in the set (the curve is *not* solid),  no further action must be taken, so we have\n\n$$\nx<2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the set as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{(x,y)\\in {Z}^{2}\\,:\\,x<2\\}\n$$",
